counterfactuals.output:
1. A DC-DC converter comprising:

a primary-side circuit configured to receive an input DC voltage;

a secondary-side circuit electrically insulated from the primary-side circuit and configured to output a converted DC voltage;

a transformer having a primary winding coupled to the primary-side circuit and a secondary winding coupled to the secondary-side circuit, the transformer providing power transfer between the primary-side circuit and the secondary-side circuit while maintaining DC isolation therebetween;

a choke coil disposed in the secondary-side circuit and coupled to the secondary winding; and

an inter-primary-side circuit wire extending between portions associated with the primary-side circuit and the secondary-side circuit, the inter-primary-side circuit wire being arranged to provide an electrical connection or reference path across the converter without forming a direct DC conductive path between the primary-side circuit and the secondary-side circuit,

wherein the primary-side circuit and the secondary-side circuit remain galvanically isolated from each other during operation of the DC-DC converter.
